xref:concat_text[The concatenation of ``text^{asterisk}^``]

. If ``text^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``""``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``text'`` be xref:concat_text[the concatenation of ``t~t~^{asterisk}^``].
 .. Return ``t~h~`` concatenated with ``text'``.

xref:join_text[The result of joining ``text''^{asterisk}^`` with separator ``t~sep~``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``text''^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
   .... Return ``""``.
  ... Else if let ``t~h~`` be ``text''^{asterisk}^``:
   .... Return ``t~h~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``t~h1~ {two-colons} text^{asterisk}^`` be ``text''^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``t~h2~ {two-colons} t~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``text^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``text'`` be xref:join_text[the result of joining ``t~h2~ {two-colons} t~t~^{asterisk}^`` with separator ``t~sep~``].
  ... Return ``t~h1~`` concatenated with ``t~sep~`` concatenated with ``text'``.

xref:replace_text[The text ``t`` with all occurrences of ``t~old~`` replaced by ``t~new~``]

. Return ``xref:replace_text'[$replace_text'(0, the length of t, t, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:replace_text'[$replace_text'(n~len''~, n~len'''~, t, t~old~, t~new~)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is equal to ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Return ``t``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is less than ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Let ``t~replaced~`` be <<ite,``t`` with ``[n~len''~]`` set to ``t~new~`` if ``t[n~len''~]`` is equal to ``t~old~`` otherwise ``t``>>.
  ... Return ``xref:replace_text'[$replace_text'(n~len''~ + 1, n~len'''~, t~replaced~, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:replace_text_except[The text ``t`` with all occurrences of ``t~old~`` not replaced by ``t~new~``]

. Return ``xref:replace_text_except'[$replace_text_except'(0, the length of t, t, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:replace_text_except'[$replace_text_except'(n~len''~, n~len'''~, t, t~old~, t~new~)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is equal to ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Return ``t``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is less than ``n~len'''~``.

  ... Let ``t~replaced~`` be <<ite,``t`` if ``t[n~len''~]`` is equal to ``t~old~`` otherwise ``t`` with ``[n~len''~]`` set to ``t~new~``>>.
  ... Return ``xref:replace_text_except'[$replace_text_except'(n~len''~ + 1, n~len'''~, t~replaced~, t~old~, t~new~)]``.

xref:strip_prefix[The text ``text`` with the prefix ``text'`` removed]

xref:strip_suffix[The text ``text`` with the suffix ``text'`` removed]

xref:strip_all_whitespace[The text ``text`` with all whitespace removed]

xref:starts_with[The text ``t`` starts with ``t~prefix~``]

. Check that the length of ``t~prefix~`` is less than or equal to the length of ``t``.

. Check that ``t[0 : the length of t~prefix~]`` is equal to ``t~prefix~``.
 return ``true``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``false``.

xref:ends_with[The text ``t`` ends with ``t~suffix~``]

. Check that the length of ``t~suffix~`` is less than or equal to the length of ``t``.

. Let ``n~start~`` be the length of ``t`` - the length of ``t~suffix~``.
. Check that ``t[n~start~ : the length of t~suffix~]`` is equal to ``t~suffix~``.
 return ``true``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``false``.

xref:strip_prefix_rec[The text ``t`` with the prefix ``t~prefix~`` removed many times as possible]

. If xref:starts_with[the text ``t`` starts with ``t~prefix~``]:
 .. Let ``t~stripped~`` be xref:strip_prefix[the text ``t`` with the prefix ``t~prefix~`` removed].
 .. Return xref:strip_prefix_rec[the text ``t~stripped~`` with the prefix ``t~prefix~`` removed many times as possible].
. Else:
 .. Return ``t``.

xref:strip_suffix_rec[The text ``t`` with the suffix ``t~suffix~`` removed many times as possible]

. If xref:ends_with[the text ``t`` ends with ``t~suffix~``]:
 .. Let ``t~stripped~`` be xref:strip_suffix[the text ``t`` with the suffix ``t~suffix~`` removed].
 .. Return xref:strip_suffix_rec[the text ``t~stripped~`` with the suffix ``t~suffix~`` removed many times as possible].
. Else:
 .. Return ``t``.

xref:contains[The text ``t`` contains ``t~c~``]

. Return ``xref:contains'[$contains'(0, the length of t, t, t~c~)]``.

xref:contains'[$contains'(n~len''~, n~len'''~, t, t~c~)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is equal to ``n~len'''~``.
 return ``false``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``n~len''~`` is less than ``n~len'''~``.

  ... If ``t[n~len''~]`` is equal to ``t~c~``: return ``true``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``xref:contains'[$contains'(n~len''~ + 1, n~len'''~, t, t~c~)]``.

xref:is_some_[$is_some_<X>(X''^?^)]

. If ``X''^?^`` matches pattern ``()``: return ``false``.
. Else: return ``true``.

xref:opt_as_seq_[$opt_as_seq_<X>(X''^?^)]

. If ``X''^?^`` matches pattern ``()``:
