xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[The expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace''``]

. If let ``literalExpression`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Return ``literalExpression``.
. Else if let ``referenceExpression`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Return ``referenceExpression``.
. Else if let ``unaryExpression`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Return ``unaryExpression``.
. Else if let ``expressionNonBrace~l~ binop expression~r~`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Let ``expression~l~`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace~l~``].
 .. Return ``expression~l~ binop expression~r~``.
. Else if let ``expressionNonBrace~cond~ +?+ expression~true~ +:+ expression~false~`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Let ``expression~cond~`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace~cond~``].
 .. Return ``expression~cond~ +?+ expression~true~ +:+ expression~false~``.
. Else if let ``castExpression`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Return ``castExpression``.
. Else if let ``errorAccessExpression`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Return ``errorAccessExpression``.
. Else if let ``memberAccessBaseNonBrace +.+ member`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. If let ``prefixedTypeName`` be ``memberAccessBaseNonBrace``:
  ... Return ``prefixedTypeName +.+ member``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``expression~base~`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace~base~``].
  ... Return ``expression~base~ +.+ member``.
. Else if let ``expressionNonBrace~base~ +[+expression~index~+]+`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. Let ``expression~base~`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace~base~``].
 .. Return ``expression~base~ +[+expression~index~+]+``.
. Else if let ``expressionNonBrace~base~ +[+expression~hi~ sliceop expression~lo~+]+`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. If ``sliceop`` matches pattern ``+:+``:
  ... Let ``expression~base~`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace~base~``].
  ... Return ``expression~base~ +[+expression~hi~ +:+ expression~lo~+]+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``expression~base~`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace~base~``].
  ... Return ``expression~base~ +[+expression~hi~ ++:+ expression~lo~+]+``.
. Else if let ``callExpressionNonBrace`` be ``expressionNonBrace''``:
 .. If let ``callTargetNonBrace +(+argumentList+)+`` be ``callExpressionNonBrace``:
  ... If let ``expressionNonBrace`` be ``callTargetNonBrace``:
   .... Let ``expression`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace``].
   .... Return ``expression +(+argumentList+)+``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``constructorTarget +(+argumentList+)+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``expression`` be xref:expressionNonBrace_as_expression[the expression corresponding to ``expressionNonBrace``].
  ... Return ``expression +<+realTypeArgumentList+>+ +(+argumentList+)+``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``parenthesizedExpression``.

xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[The non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression''``]

. If let ``literalExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Return ``literalExpression``.
. Else if let ``referenceExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Return ``referenceExpression``.
. Else if let ``unaryExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Return ``unaryExpression``.
. Else if let ``expression~l~ binop expression~r~`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Let ``expressionNonBrace~l~`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression~l~``].
 .. Return ``expressionNonBrace~l~ binop expression~r~``.
. Else if let ``expression~cond~ +?+ expression~true~ +:+ expression~false~`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Let ``expressionNonBrace~cond~`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression~cond~``].
 .. Return ``expressionNonBrace~cond~ +?+ expression~true~ +:+ expression~false~``.
. Else if let ``castExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Return ``castExpression``.
. Else if let ``errorAccessExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Return ``errorAccessExpression``.
. Else if let ``memberAccessBase +.+ member`` be ``expression''``:
 .. If let ``prefixedTypeName`` be ``memberAccessBase``:
  ... Return ``prefixedTypeName +.+ member``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``expressionNonBrace~base~`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression~base~``].
  ... Return ``expressionNonBrace~base~ +.+ member``.
. Else if let ``expression~base~ +[+expression~index~+]+`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Let ``expressionNonBrace~base~`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression~base~``].
 .. Return ``expressionNonBrace~base~ +[+expression~index~+]+``.
. Else if let ``expression~base~ +[+expression~hi~ sliceop expression~lo~+]+`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Check that ``sliceop`` matches pattern ``+:+``.

 .. Let ``expressionNonBrace~base~`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression~base~``].
 .. Return ``expressionNonBrace~base~ +[+expression~hi~ +:+ expression~lo~+]+``.
. Else if let ``callExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. If let ``callTarget +(+argumentList+)+`` be ``callExpression``:
  ... If let ``expression`` be ``callTarget``:
   .... Let ``expressionNonBrace`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression``].
   .... Return ``expressionNonBrace +(+argumentList+)+``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``constructorTarget +(+argumentList+)+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``expressionNonBrace`` be xref:expression_as_expressionNonBrace[the non-brace expression corresponding to ``expression``].
  ... Return ``expressionNonBrace +<+realTypeArgumentList+>+ +(+argumentList+)+``.
. Else if let ``parenthesizedExpression`` be ``expression''``:
 .. Return ``parenthesizedExpression``.

