. Let ``bound`` be xref:free_typeIR[free type identifiers in ``typeIR~free~``], for all ``typeIR~free~`` in ``typeIR~free~^{asterisk}^`` and ``bound`` in ``bound^{asterisk}^``.
. Let ``B~capture~`` be xref:unions_set[the union of the sets ``bound^{asterisk}^``].
. Let ``typeId~fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:fresh_typeIds[the length of ``typeParameterIR~expl~^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``typeParameterIR~impl~^{asterisk}^`` fresh type variables].
. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<typeId>(typeId~fresh~, B~capture~)]``, for all ``typeId~fresh~`` in ``typeId~fresh~^{asterisk}^``.

. Let ``typeParameterIR~expl_fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeId~fresh~^{asterisk}^[0 : the length of typeParameterIR~expl~^{asterisk}^]``.
. Let ``typeParameterIR~impl_fresh~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeId~fresh~^{asterisk}^[the length of typeParameterIR~expl~^{asterisk}^ : the length of typeParameterIR~impl~^{asterisk}^]``.
. Let ``theta~fresh~`` be xref:adds_map[``theta`` where each of ``typeParameterIR~expl~^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``typeParameterIR~impl~^{asterisk}^`` to ``typeParameterIR~expl_fresh~^{asterisk}^`` concatenated with ``typeParameterIR~impl_fresh~^{asterisk}^`` are added].
. Return ( ``theta~fresh~``, ``typeParameterIR~expl_fresh~^{asterisk}^``, ``typeParameterIR~impl_fresh~^{asterisk}^`` ).

