xref:un_op[``unop`` ``value``]

. If ``unop`` matches pattern ``+~+``:
 .. Return xref:un_bnot[``+~+`` ``value``].
. Else if ``unop`` matches pattern ``+!+``:
 .. Return xref:un_lnot[``+!+`` ``value``].
. Else if ``unop`` matches pattern ``+++``:
 .. Return xref:un_plus[``+++`` ``value``].
. Else:
 .. Return xref:un_minus[``+-+`` ``value``].

xref:un_bnot[``+~+`` ``value``]

. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``value``.

. If let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:bneg[the two's complement negation of ``i``].
 .. Let ``int`` be xref:pow2[2 to the power of ``w``].
 .. Let ``i''`` be xref:ite[``i'`` if ``i'`` is greater than or equal to ``0`` otherwise ``int`` + ``i'``].
 .. Return ``w +W+ i''``.
. Else if let ``w +S+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:bneg[the two's complement negation of ``i``].
 .. Let ``int'`` be xref:pow2[2 to the power of ``w``].
 .. Let ``i''`` be xref:ite[``i'`` if ``i'`` is greater than or equal to ``0`` otherwise ``int'`` + ``i'``].
 .. Return ``w +S+ i''``.

xref:un_lnot[``+!+`` ``value``]

. Let!~type~ ``b`` be ``value``.

. Return ``~b``.

xref:un_plus[``+++`` ``value``]

. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``value``.

. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Return ``+D+ i``.
. Else if let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Return ``w +W+ i``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``w +S+ i``.

xref:un_minus[``+-+`` ``value``]

. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``value``.

. If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Return ``+D+ -i``.
. Else if let ``w +W+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let ``int`` be xref:pow2[2 to the power of ``w``].
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w`` representing the integer ``int`` - ``i``].
 .. Return ``w +W+ i'``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``int'`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``-i`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w`` representing the integer ``int'``].
 .. Return ``w +S+ i'``.

xref:bin_op[``value~l~`` ``binop`` ``value~r~``]

. If ``binop`` matches pattern ``+++``:
 .. Return xref:bin_plus[``value~l~`` ``+++`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+|+|+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_satplus[``value~l~`` ``+|+|+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+-+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_minus[``value~l~`` ``+-+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+|-|+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_satminus[``value~l~`` ``+|-|+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+*+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_mul[``value~l~`` ``+*+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+/+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_div[``value~l~`` ``+/+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+%+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_mod[``value~l~`` ``+%+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+<<+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_shl[``value~l~`` ``+<<+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+>>+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_shr[``value~l~`` ``+>>+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+<=+``:
 .. Let ``bool`` be xref:bin_le[``value~l~`` ``+<=+`` ``value~r~``].
 .. Return ``bool``.
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+>=+``:
 .. Let ``bool'`` be xref:bin_ge[``value~l~`` ``+>=+`` ``value~r~``].
 .. Return ``bool'``.
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+<+``:
 .. Let ``bool''`` be xref:bin_lt[``value~l~`` ``+<+`` ``value~r~``].
 .. Return ``bool''``.
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+>+``:
 .. Let ``bool'''`` be xref:bin_gt[``value~l~`` ``+>+`` ``value~r~``].
 .. Return ``bool'''``.
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+==+``:
 .. Let ``bool''''`` be xref:bin_eq[``value~l~`` ``+==+`` ``value~r~``].
 .. Return ``bool''''``.
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+!=+``:
 .. Let ``bool'''''`` be xref:bin_ne[``value~l~`` ``+!=+`` ``value~r~``].
 .. Return ``bool'''''``.
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+&+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_band[``value~l~`` ``+&+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+^+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_bxor[``value~l~`` ``+^+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+|+``:
 .. Return xref:bin_bor[``value~l~`` ``+|+`` ``value~r~``].
. Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``++++``:
 .. Return xref:bin_concat[``value~l~`` ``++++`` ``value~r~``].

xref:bin_plus[``value`` ``+++`` ``value'``]

. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``value``.

. If let ``+D+ i~l~`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``+D+ i~r~`` be ``integerLiteral'``.

 .. Return ``+D+ i~l~ + i~r~``.
. Else if let ``w +W+ i~l~`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``w' +W+ i~r~`` be ``integerLiteral'``.

 .. Check that ``w`` is equal to ``w'``.

 .. Let ``i~l'~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i~l~`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i~r'~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i~r~`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w`` representing the integer ``i~l'~`` + ``i~r'~``].
 .. Return ``w +W+ i'``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``w' +S+ i~r~`` be ``integerLiteral'``.

 .. Check that ``w`` is equal to ``w'``.

 .. Let ``i~l'~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i~l~`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i~r'~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i~r~`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w`` representing the integer ``i~l'~`` + ``i~r'~``].
 .. Return ``w +S+ i'``.

xref:bin_satplus[``value`` ``+|+|+`` ``value'``]

. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``value``.

. If let ``w +W+ i~l~`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``w' +W+ i~r~`` be ``integerLiteral'``.

 .. Check that ``w`` is equal to ``w'``.

 .. Let ``i`` be ``i~l~`` + ``i~r~``.
 .. Let ``i~max~`` be xref:pow2[2 to the power of ``w``].
 .. Let ``i'`` be xref:ite[``i`` if ``i`` is less than ``i~max~`` otherwise ``i~max~`` - ``1``].
 .. Return ``w +W+ i'``.
. Else if let ``w +S+ i~l~`` be ``integerLiteral``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral'`` be ``value'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``w'' +S+ i~r~`` be ``integerLiteral'``.

 .. Check that ``w`` is equal to ``w''``.

 .. Let ``i~l'~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i~l~`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i~r'~`` be xref:bitstr_to_int[the two's complement representation of bitstring ``i~r~`` of width ``w``].
 .. Let ``i'`` be ``i~l'~`` + ``i~r'~``.
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``i'`` is greater than ``0``.

   .... Let ``w'`` be ``w`` - ``1``.
   .... Let ``i~max~`` be xref:pow2[2 to the power of ``w'``].
   .... Let ``i''`` be xref:ite[``i'`` if ``i'`` is less than ``i~max~`` otherwise ``i~max~`` - ``1``].
   .... Let ``i'''`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w`` representing the integer ``i''``].
   .... Return ``w +S+ i'''``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``i'`` is less than or equal to ``0``.

   .... Let ``w'`` be ``w`` - ``1``.
   .... Let ``int`` be xref:pow2[2 to the power of ``w'``].
   .... Let ``i~min~`` be ``-int``.
   .... Let ``i''`` be xref:ite[``i'`` if ``i'`` is greater than or equal to ``i~min~`` otherwise ``i~min~``].
   .... Let ``i'''`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``w`` representing the integer ``i''``].
   .... Return ``w +S+ i'''``.

