 .. Else:
  ... Let ``callableTypeDefEnv`` be ``TC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+``.
  ... Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
  ... Return xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``callableTypeDefEnv`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_callableTypeDefIR``].
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. If let ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
  ... Let ``callableTypeDefEnv`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+``.
  ... Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let ``callableId +:+ callableTypeDefIR +#+ id~default~^{asterisk}^ +#+ id~optional~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``callableTypeDefEnv`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_callableTypeDefIR``].
    ..... Return ``callableId +:+ callableTypeDefIR +#+ id~default~^{asterisk}^ +#+ id~optional~^{asterisk}^``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``callableTypeDefEnv`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_callableTypeDefIR``].

    ..... Return xref:find_callableDef_overloaded_t[the overloaded callable definition of ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer of ``TC``].
