  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let ``( callableId, callableTypeDefIR )`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<callableTypeDefIR>(TC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+, nameIR)]``.
     ...... Return ( ``callableId``, ``callableTypeDefIR`` ).
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<callableTypeDefIR>(TC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+, nameIR)]``.

     ...... Return xref:find_callableDef_non_overloaded_t[the non-overloaded callable definition of ``nameIR`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer of ``TC``].
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Return xref:find_callableDef_non_overloaded_t[the non-overloaded callable definition of ``nameIR`` from the ``+BLOCK+`` layer of ``TC``].

xref:find_constructorDef_overloaded_t[The overloaded constructor definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` in ``TC``]

. If let ``+.+ nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
