xref:find_local_return_type_t[The expected return type in ``TC``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
  ... If let ``+FUNCTION+ +:+ typeIR~ret~`` be ``localKind``:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``+ACTION+`` is equal to ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.

  ... Return ``+VOID+``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``externMethodLocalKind`` be ``localKind``.

  ... If let ``+EXTERN_METHOD+ +:+ typeIR~ret~`` be ``externMethodLocalKind``:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
  ... Else:
   .... Return ``typeIR~ret~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+`` is equal to ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.

  ... Return ``+VOID+``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``·``.

xref:empty_tableContext[$empty_tableContext]

. Let ``matchPriority`` be +{++DELTA+ ``1``, +LARGEST_WINS+ ``true``+}+.
. Let ``matchEntries`` be +{++SIZE+ ``0``, +CONST+ ``true``+}+.
. Return +{++KEYS+ ``·``, +ACTIONS+ ``·``, +PRIORITIES+ ``matchPriority``, +ENTRIES+ ``matchEntries``, +MODE+ ``+NONE+``+}+.

xref:add_key_tbl[``TBLC`` with match key ``id`` of type ``typeIR`` added]

. Let ``matchKey`` be ``typeIR +:+ id``.
. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+KEYS+`` set to ``TBLC.+KEYS+ {pp} matchKey``.

xref:add_action_tbl[``TBLC`` with match action ``prefixedNameIR`` ``+(+`` ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` applied using ``argumentListIR`` added]

. Let ``matchAction`` be ``prefixedNameIR +(+parameterIR^{asterisk}^ +@+ argumentListIR+)+``.
. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+ACTIONS+`` set to ``TBLC.+ACTIONS+ {pp} matchAction``.

xref:is_lpm_key[Match kind of table key ``++_++ +#+ ++_++ +:+ nameIR ++_++ +;+`` is lpm]

. Return ``xref:is_lpm_key'[$is_lpm_key'(nameIR)]``.

xref:is_lpm_key'[$is_lpm_key'(text')]

. Check that ``text'`` is equal to ``"lpm"``.
 return ``true``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``false``.

xref:requires_priority[Match kind of table key ``++_++ +#+ ++_++ +:+ nameIR ++_++ +;+`` requires a priority]

. Return ``xref:requires_priority'[$requires_priority'(nameIR)]``.

xref:requires_priority'[$requires_priority'(text')]

. If ``text'`` is equal to ``"range"``: return ``true``.
. Else if ``text'`` is equal to ``"ternary"``: return ``true``.
. Else: return ``true``.

. Otherwise:
 .. Otherwise:
  ... Return ``false``.

xref:update_mode_tbl[``TBLC`` with match mode updated based on keys ``tableKeyIR^{asterisk}^``]

. Let ``b~pri~`` be xref:requires_priority[match kind of table key ``tableKeyIR`` requires a priority], for all ``tableKeyIR`` in ``tableKeyIR^{asterisk}^`` and ``b~pri~`` in ``b~pri~^{asterisk}^``.
. If xref:exists_[some of ``b~pri~^{asterisk}^`` is true]:
 .. Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+PRI+``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``b~lpm~`` be xref:is_lpm_key[match kind of table key ``tableKeyIR`` is lpm], for all ``tableKeyIR`` in ``tableKeyIR^{asterisk}^`` and ``b~lpm~`` in ``b~lpm~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Let ``tableKeyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``tableKeyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``b~lpm~^{asterisk}^``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``tableKeyIR~lpm~`` be ``tableKeyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR +#+ ++_++ +:+ text ++_++ +;+`` be ``tableKeyIR~lpm~``.
   .... Check that ``text`` is equal to ``"lpm"``.

   .... Let ``typeIR`` be xref:type_of_typedExpressionIR[the type of ``typedExpressionIR``].
   .... Let ``typeIR'`` be xref:unroll_aliasTypeIR[``typeIR`` with aliases unrolled].
   .... Let!~type~ ``integerTypeIR`` be ``typeIR'``.

   .... Let ``n`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:width_of_integerTypeIR[width of integer type ``integerTypeIR``].
   .... Return ``TBLC`` with ``+MODE+`` set to ``+LPM+ n``.
