xref:set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR[``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^`` with priorities set based on table context ``TBLC`` and entry states ``TBLS^{asterisk}^``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+NONE+``.

  ... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR``], for all ``tableEntryIR`` in ``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Return ``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``matchMode`` be ``TBLC.+MODE+``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``+LPM+ n`` be ``matchMode``.

  ... Check that ``TBLS`` matches pattern ``+LPM+ %``, for all ``TBLS`` in ``TBLS^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``+LPM+ n~prefix~`` be ``TBLS``, for all ``TBLS`` in ``TBLS^{asterisk}^`` and ``n~prefix~`` in ``n~prefix~^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR``], for all ``tableEntryIR`` in ``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``tableEntryIR~updated~`` be ``xref:set_priority_of_tableEntryIR[$set_priority_of_tableEntryIR(tableEntryIR, n~prefix~)]``, for all ``n~prefix~`` in ``n~prefix~^{asterisk}^``, ``tableEntryIR`` in ``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^``, and ``tableEntryIR~updated~`` in ``tableEntryIR~updated~^{asterisk}^``.
  ... Return ``tableEntryIR~updated~^{asterisk}^``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
   .... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+PRI+``.

   .... Return ``·``.
  ... Else:
   .... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` matches pattern ``+PRI+``.

   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR~h~``].

     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR~t~``], for all ``tableEntryIR~t~`` in ``tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^``.

     ...... Let ``b~lw~`` be ``TBLC.+PRIORITIES+.+LARGEST_WINS+``.
     ...... Let ``n~size~`` be ``TBLC.+ENTRIES+.+SIZE+``.
     ...... Let ``n~delta~`` be ``TBLC.+PRIORITIES+.+DELTA+``.
     ...... Let ``int`` be xref:ite[``n~size~ - 1 * n~delta~ + 1`` if ``b~lw~`` otherwise ``1``].
     ...... Let!~type~ ``n`` be ``int``.

     ...... Let ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~`` be ``xref:set_priority_of_tableEntryIR[$set_priority_of_tableEntryIR(tableEntryIR~h~, n)]``.
     ...... Let ``tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'[$set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'(TBLC, n, tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
     ...... Return ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~ {two-colons} tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that not ``TBLC.+ENTRIES+.+CONST+``.

     ...... Let ``+PRIORITY+ +=+ integerLiteral +:+`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR~h~``].
     ...... Let ``n`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerLiteral``].
     ...... Let ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~`` be ``xref:set_priority_of_tableEntryIR[$set_priority_of_tableEntryIR(tableEntryIR~h~, n)]``.
     ...... Let ``tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'[$set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'(TBLC, n, tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
     ...... Return ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~ {two-colons} tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'[$set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'(TBLC, n~last~, tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``tableEntryIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Return ``·``.
. Else:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR~h~``].

   .... Let ``b~lw~`` be ``TBLC.+PRIORITIES+.+LARGEST_WINS+``.
   .... Let ``n~delta~`` be ``TBLC.+PRIORITIES+.+DELTA+``.
   .... Let ``int`` be xref:ite[``n~last~ - n~delta~`` if ``b~lw~`` otherwise ``n~last~ + n~delta~``].
   .... Let!~type~ ``n`` be ``int``.

   .... Let ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~`` be ``xref:set_priority_of_tableEntryIR[$set_priority_of_tableEntryIR(tableEntryIR~h~, n)]``.
   .... Let ``tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'[$set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'(TBLC, n, tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
   .... Return ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~ {two-colons} tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Let ``+PRIORITY+ +=+ integerLiteral +:+`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:tableEntryPriorityOptIR_of_tableEntryIR[the priority of ``tableEntryIR~h~``].
   .... Let ``n`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerLiteral``].
   .... Let ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~`` be ``xref:set_priority_of_tableEntryIR[$set_priority_of_tableEntryIR(tableEntryIR~h~, n)]``.
   .... Let ``tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^`` be ``xref:set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'[$set_priorities_of_tableEntryListIR'(TBLC, n, tableEntryIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
   .... Return ``tableEntryIR~h_updated~ {two-colons} tableEntryIR~t_updated~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:set_priority_of_tableEntryIR[$set_priority_of_tableEntryIR(tableEntryIR, n)]

. Let ``constOptIR ++_++ keysetExpressionIR +:+ tableActionReferenceIR annotationList +;+`` be ``tableEntryIR``.
. Let ``tableEntryPriorityIR`` be ``+PRIORITY+ +=+ +D+ n +:+``.
. Let ``tableEntryIR~updated~`` be ``constOptIR tableEntryPriorityIR keysetExpressionIR +:+ tableActionReferenceIR annotationList +;+``.
. Return ``tableEntryIR~updated~``.

xref:join_tableEntryState[$join_tableEntryState(tableEntryState, tableEntryState')]

. If ``tableEntryState`` matches pattern ``+NON_LPM+``:
 .. If let ``+LPM+ n`` be ``tableEntryState'``:
  ... Return ``+LPM+ n``.
 .. Else:
  ... Return ``+NON_LPM+``.
. Else:
 .. Check that ``tableEntryState'`` matches pattern ``+NON_LPM+``.

 .. Return ``+LPM+ n``.

xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix(value)]

. Return ``xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value, 0)]``.

xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value, n~prefix'~)]

. Let!~type~ ``integerLiteral`` be ``value``.

. Let!~type~ ``nat +W+ ++_++`` be ``integerLiteral``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``nat`` is equal to ``0``.

  ... Return ``n~prefix'~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``n`` be ``++_++``.

  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``nat`` is greater than ``0``.

    ..... Let ``w'`` be ``nat`` - ``1``.
    ..... Check that ``n`` \ ``2`` is not equal to ``0``.

    ..... Let ``n'`` be ``n`` - ``1`` / ``2``.
    ..... Let ``value'`` be ``w' +W+ n'``.
    ..... Return ``xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value', n~prefix'~ + 1)]``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``n~prefix'~`` is equal to ``0``.

    ..... Check that ``nat`` is greater than ``0``.

    ..... Let ``w'`` be ``nat`` - ``1``.
    ..... Check that ``n`` \ ``2`` is equal to ``0``.

    ..... Let ``value'`` be ``w' +W+ n / 2``.
    ..... Return ``xref:tableEntry_lpm_prefix'[$tableEntry_lpm_prefix'(value', 0)]``.

xref:Type_wf[Type_wf]:

* ``typeIR''`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``

. If let ``baseTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. The relation holds.
. Else if let ``typeId`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:in_set[``typeId`` is an element of the set ``B``].

 .. The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+TYPEDEF+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:nestable_typedef[``typeIR`` can be used in a typedef].

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+TYPE+ ++_++ typeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:nestable_new[``typeIR`` can be used in a new type].

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+LIST+ +<+typeIR+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:nestable_list[``typeIR`` can be nested in a list type].

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+TUPLE+ +<+typeIR^{asterisk}^+>+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:nestable_tuple[``typeIR`` can be nested in a tuple type], for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+ARRAY+ typeIR +[+++_+++]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:nestable_array[``typeIR`` can be nested in an array type].

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_STACK+ typeIR +[+++_+++]+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:nestable_headerStack[``typeIR`` can be nested in a header stack type].

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+STRUCT+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:distinct_[the elements of ``nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`` are distinct].

 .. Check that xref:nestable_struct[``typeIR~field~`` can be nested in a struct type], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``.

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR~field~`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+HEADER+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:distinct_[the elements of ``nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`` are distinct].

 .. Check that xref:nestable_header[``typeIR~field~`` can be used in a header type], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``.

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR~field~`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+HEADER_UNION+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ typeIR~field~ nameIR~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:distinct_[the elements of ``nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`` are distinct].

 .. Check that xref:nestable_headerUnion[``typeIR~field~`` can be used in a header union type], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``.

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR~field~`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``typeIR~field~`` in ``typeIR~field~^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+ENUM+ ++_++ +{+nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:distinct_[the elements of ``nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`` are distinct].

 .. The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+ENUM+ ++_++ +<+typeIR+>+ +{+( nameIR~field~ +=+ ++_++ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that xref:distinct_[the elements of ``nameIR~field~^{asterisk}^`` are distinct].

 .. Check that xref:nestable_enum_serializable[``typeIR`` can be used in a serializable enum type].

 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+EXTERN+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+( ++_++ +:+ externMethodTypeDefIR )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If xref:CallableTypeDef_wf[``externMethodTypeDefIR`` is a well-formed callable type definition, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``externMethodTypeDefIR`` in ``externMethodTypeDefIR^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+PARSER+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +(+parameterIR^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If xref:ParameterType_wf[``parameterIR`` is a well-formed parameter, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+CONTROL+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +(+parameterIR^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If xref:ParameterType_wf[``parameterIR`` is a well-formed parameter, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+PACKAGE+ ++_++ +<+++_++^{asterisk}^+>+ +{+typeIR^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``], for all ``typeIR`` in ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``+TABLE+ ++_++ +{+tableMetadataStructTypeIR+}+`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. If xref:Type_wf[``tableMetadataStructTypeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``B``]:
  ... The relation holds.
. Else if let ``defaultTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``defaultTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+DEFAULT+``.

 .. The relation holds.
. Else if let ``invalidHeaderTypeIR`` be ``typeIR''``:
 .. Check that ``invalidHeaderTypeIR`` matches pattern ``+HEADER_INVALID+``.

 .. The relation holds.
