xref:Expr_eval_lctk[Expr_eval_lctk]:

* Local compile-time evaluation of xref:typedExpressionIR[``expressionIR`` annotated with ``++_++``], under context ``TC`` at ``p``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``booleanLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Let ``boolValue`` be xref:ite[``true`` if ``booleanLiteral`` is equal to ``+TRUE+`` otherwise ``false``].
   .... Result in ``boolValue``.
  ... Else if let ``integerLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Result in ``integerLiteral``.
  ... Else if let ``stringLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Result in ``stringLiteral``.
  ... Else if let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Let ``value`` be xref:find_var_value_t[the value of variable ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p`` layer of ``TC``].
   .... Result in ``value``.
  ... Else if let ``defaultExpression`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Check that ``defaultExpression`` matches pattern ``+...+``.

   .... Result in ``+DEFAULT+``.
  ... Else if let ``unop typedExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in xref:un_op[``unop`` ``value``].
  ... Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~l~ binop typedExpressionIR~r~`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``binop`` is not in ``+[+ +&&+, +||+ +]+``.

     ...... Let ``value~l~`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
     ...... Let ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
     ...... Result in xref:bin_op[``value~l~`` ``binop`` ``value~r~``].
    ..... {empty}
     ...... If ``binop`` matches pattern ``+&&+``:
      ....... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
      ....... Try:
       ........ {empty}
        ......... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

        ......... Result in ``false``.
       ........ {empty}
        ......... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

        ......... Let ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
        ......... Result in ``value~r~``.
     ...... Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+||+``:
      ....... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
      ....... Try:
       ........ {empty}
        ......... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

        ......... Result in ``true``.
       ........ {empty}
        ......... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

        ......... Let ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
        ......... Result in ``value~r~``.
  ... Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~cond~ +?+ typedExpressionIR~true~ +:+ typedExpressionIR~false~`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~cond~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

     ...... Let ``value~true~`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~true~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
     ...... Result in ``value~true~``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

     ...... Let ``value~false~`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~false~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
     ...... Result in ``value~false~``.
  ... Else if let ``+(+typeIR+)+ typedExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
   .... Let ``value~cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
   .... Result in ``value~cast~``.
  ... Else if let ``invalidHeaderExpression`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... Check that ``invalidHeaderExpression`` matches pattern ``+{#}+``.

   .... Result in ``+{#}+``.
  ... Else if let ``sequenceExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... If let ``+SEQ+ +{+typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``sequenceExpressionIR``:
    ..... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``], for all ``typedExpressionIR`` in ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`` and ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... Result in ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``], for all ``typedExpressionIR`` in ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`` and ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... Result in ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^ +,+ +...++)+``.
  ... Else if let ``recordExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
   .... If let ``+RECORD+ +{+( nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``recordExpressionIR``:
    ..... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``], for all ``typedExpressionIR`` in ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`` and ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... Result in ``+RECORD+ +{+( value nameIR +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_eval_lctk[local compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``], for all ``typedExpressionIR`` in ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`` and ``value`` in ``value^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... Result in ``+RECORD+ +{+( value nameIR +;+ )^{asterisk}^ +,+ +...++}+``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``+(+++_++ ++_+++)+`` be ``++_++``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``+ERROR+ +.+ nameIR`` be ``expressionIR``.

  ... Let ``nameIR~error~`` be ``"error."`` concatenated with ``nameIR``.
  ... Let ``value~error~`` be xref:find_var_value_t[the value of variable ``nameIR~error~`` from the ``p`` layer of ``TC``].
