* Typing ``expression'''``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``booleanLiteral`` be ``expression'''``:
   .... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``+BOOL+`` and compile-time known-ness ``+LCTK+``].
   .... Result in xref:typedExpressionIR[``booleanLiteral`` annotated with ``expressionNoteIR``].
  ... Else if let ``integerLiteral`` be ``expression'''``:
   .... If let ``+D+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
    ..... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``+INT+`` and compile-time known-ness ``+LCTK+``].
    ..... Result in xref:typedExpressionIR[``+D+ i`` annotated with ``expressionNoteIR``].
   .... Else if let ``n +S+ i`` be ``integerLiteral``:
    ..... Let ``i~norm~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``n`` representing the integer ``i``].
    ..... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``+INT+ +<+n+>+`` and compile-time known-ness ``+LCTK+``].
    ..... Check that ``n`` is greater than ``0``.

    ..... Result in xref:typedExpressionIR[``n +S+ i~norm~`` annotated with ``expressionNoteIR``].
   .... Else:
    ..... Let ``i~norm~`` be xref:int_to_bitstr[the bitstring of width ``n`` representing the integer ``i``].
    ..... Let ``expressionNoteIR`` be xref:expressionNoteIR[a pair of type ``+BIT+ +<+n+>+`` and compile-time known-ness ``+LCTK+``].
    ..... Result in xref:typedExpressionIR[``n +W+ i~norm~`` annotated with ``expressionNoteIR``].
