xref:ParserTransition_ok[ParserTransition_ok]:

* Typing ``transitionStatement``, under context ``TC~0~`` and parser state names ``nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^``.

. If ``transitionStatement`` matches pattern ````:
 .. Result in typed transition statement ``+TRANSITION+ "reject" +;+``.
. Else:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``name +;+`` be ``stateExpression``.

   .... Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``name``].
   .... Check that ``nameIR`` is in ``nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^``.

   .... Let ``transitionStatementIR`` be ``+TRANSITION+ nameIR +;+``.
   .... Result in typed transition statement ``transitionStatementIR``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``selectExpression`` be ``stateExpression``.

   .... Let typed transition statement ``selectExpressionIR`` be the result of xref:ParserSelect_ok[typing ``selectExpression``, under context ``TC~0~`` and parser state names ``nameIR~state~^{asterisk}^``].
   .... Result in typed transition statement ``+TRANSITION+ selectExpressionIR``.

xref:ParserStmt_ok[ParserStmt_ok]:

* Typing ``parserStatement``, under context ``TC'``.

. If let ``emptyStatement`` be ``parserStatement``:
 .. Let context ``typingContext`` and ``statementIR`` be the result of xref:Stmt_ok[typing ``emptyStatement``, under context ``TC'`` at ``+LOCAL+``].
 .. Check that ``typingContext`` is equal to ``TC'``.

 .. Let!~type~ ``emptyStatementIR`` be ``statementIR``.

 .. Result in context ``TC'`` and typed parser statement ``emptyStatementIR``.
. Else if let ``assignmentStatement`` be ``parserStatement``:
 .. Let context ``TC~1~`` and ``statementIR`` be the result of xref:Stmt_ok[typing ``assignmentStatement``, under context ``TC'`` at ``+LOCAL+``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``assignmentStatementIR`` be ``statementIR``.

 .. Result in context ``TC~1~`` and typed parser statement ``assignmentStatementIR``.
. Else if let ``callStatement`` be ``parserStatement``:
 .. Let context ``TC~1~`` and ``statementIR`` be the result of xref:Stmt_ok[typing ``callStatement``, under context ``TC'`` at ``+LOCAL+``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``callStatementIR`` be ``statementIR``.

 .. Result in context ``TC~1~`` and typed parser statement ``callStatementIR``.
. Else if let ``directApplicationStatement`` be ``parserStatement``:
 .. Let context ``TC~1~`` and ``statementIR`` be the result of xref:Stmt_ok[typing ``directApplicationStatement``, under context ``TC'`` at ``+LOCAL+``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``directApplicationStatementIR`` be ``statementIR``.

 .. Result in context ``TC~1~`` and typed parser statement ``directApplicationStatementIR``.
. Else if let ``parserBlockStatement`` be ``parserStatement``:
 .. Let ``TC~1~`` be xref:enter_t[``TC'`` with a new local frame].
 .. Let context ``TC~2~`` and ``parserBlockStatementIR`` be the result of xref:ParserBlock_ok[typing ``parserBlockStatement`` under context ``TC~1~``].
 .. Let ``TC~3~`` be xref:exit_t[``TC~2~`` with the innermost frame removed].
 .. Result in context ``TC~3~`` and typed parser statement ``parserBlockStatementIR``.
. Else:
 .. If let ``+IF+ +(+expression~cond~+)+ parserStatement~then~`` be ``parserConditionalStatement``:
  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~cond~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression~cond~``, under context ``TC'`` at ``+LOCAL+``].
  ... Let ``typeIR~cond~`` be xref:type_of_typedExpressionIR[the type of ``typedExpressionIR~cond~``].
  ... Check that ``+BOOL+`` is equal to xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR~cond~`` with typedefs unrolled].

  ... Let context ``TC~then~`` and typed parser statement ``parserStatementIR~then~`` be the result of xref:ParserStmt_ok[typing ``parserStatement~then~``, under context ``TC'``].
  ... Result in context ``TC'`` and typed parser statement ``+IF+ +(+typedExpressionIR~cond~+)+ parserStatementIR~then~``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~cond~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression~cond~``, under context ``TC'`` at ``+LOCAL+``].
  ... Let ``typeIR~cond~`` be xref:type_of_typedExpressionIR[the type of ``typedExpressionIR~cond~``].
  ... Check that ``+BOOL+`` is equal to xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR~cond~`` with typedefs unrolled].

  ... Let context ``TC~then~`` and typed parser statement ``parserStatementIR~then~`` be the result of xref:ParserStmt_ok[typing ``parserStatement~then~``, under context ``TC'``].
  ... Let context ``TC~else~`` and typed parser statement ``parserStatementIR~else~`` be the result of xref:ParserStmt_ok[typing ``parserStatement~else~``, under context ``TC'``].
  ... Result in context ``TC'`` and typed parser statement ``+IF+ +(+typedExpressionIR~cond~+)+ parserStatementIR~then~ +ELSE+ parserStatementIR~else~``.

xref:ParserBlockElementStmt_ok[ParserBlockElementStmt_ok]:

