   .... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR``.
  ... Else if let ``tupleKeysetExpression`` be ``keysetExpression``:
   .... If let ``+(+expression~l~ +&&&+ expression~r~+)+`` be ``tupleKeysetExpression``:
    ..... Check that the length of ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` is equal to ``1``.

    ..... Let table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok[typing ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` against ``expression~l~ +&&&+ expression~r~`` under context ``TC``, table context ``TBLC``, and table entry state ``+NON_LPM+``].
    ..... Let!~type~ ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR`` be ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^``.

    ..... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+)+``.
   .... Else if let ``+(+expression~l~ +..+ expression~r~+)+`` be ``tupleKeysetExpression``:
    ..... Check that the length of ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` is equal to ``1``.

    ..... Let table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok[typing ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` against ``expression~l~ +..+ expression~r~`` under context ``TC``, table context ``TBLC``, and table entry state ``+NON_LPM+``].
    ..... Let!~type~ ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR`` be ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR'^{asterisk}^``.

    ..... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(+simpleKeysetExpressionIR+)+``.
   .... Else if ``tupleKeysetExpression`` matches pattern ``+(++DEFAULT++)+``:
    ..... Try:
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Let ``matchMode`` be ``TBLC.+MODE+``.
      ....... Let!~type~ ``+LPM+ n`` be ``matchMode``.

      ....... Let ``TBLS`` be ``+LPM+ n``.
      ....... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(++DEFAULT++)+``.
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` is equal to ``+NONE+`` or ``TBLC.+MODE+`` is equal to ``+PRI+``.

      ....... Let ``TBLS`` be ``+NON_LPM+``.
      ....... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(++DEFAULT++)+``.
   .... Else if ``tupleKeysetExpression`` matches pattern ``+(++_++)+``:
    ..... Try:
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Let ``matchMode`` be ``TBLC.+MODE+``.
      ....... Let!~type~ ``+LPM+ n`` be ``matchMode``.

      ....... Let ``TBLS`` be ``+LPM+ 0``.
      ....... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(++_++)+``.
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``TBLC.+MODE+`` is equal to ``+NONE+`` or ``TBLC.+MODE+`` is equal to ``+PRI+``.

      ....... Let ``TBLS`` be ``+NON_LPM+``.
      ....... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(++_++)+``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let ``simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^`` be xref:flatten_simpleKeysetExpressionList[``simpleKeysetExpressionList~t~`` flattened].
    ..... Let ``simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`` be ``simpleKeysetExpression~h~ {two-colons} simpleKeysetExpression~t~^{asterisk}^``.
    ..... Check that the length of ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` is equal to the length of ``simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^``.

    ..... Let table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:TableEntry_keysets_simple_ok[typing ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` against ``simpleKeysetExpression^{asterisk}^`` under context ``TC``, table context ``TBLC``, and table entry state ``+NON_LPM+``].
    ..... Result in table entry state ``TBLS`` and ``+(+simpleKeysetExpressionIR^{asterisk}^+)+``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``simpleKeysetExpression`` be ``keysetExpression``.

  ... If let ``expression~l~ +&&&+ expression~r~`` be ``simpleKeysetExpression``:
   .... Check that the length of ``TBLC.+KEYS+`` is equal to ``1``.

