xref:VarDecl_ok[VarDecl_ok]:

* Typing ``annotationList type name initializerOpt +;+``, under context ``TC~0~`` at ``p``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``initializerOpt`` matches pattern ````.

  ... Let ``typeIR`` and fresh type variables ``typeId^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Type_ok[typing ``type``, under context ``TC~0~`` at ``p``].
  ... Check that ``typeId^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

  ... Let ``bound`` be xref:bound[bound type variables from the ``p`` layer of ``TC~0~``].
  ... If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``bound``]:
   .... Check that xref:is_assignable_typeIR[``typeIR`` supports assignment].

   .... Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``name``].
   .... Let ``TC~1~`` be xref:add_var_t[``TC~0~`` where ``nameIR`` to ``+INOUT+ typeIR +DYN+ ·`` is added to the ``p`` layer].
   .... Let ``variableDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR nameIR · +;+``.
   .... Result in context ``TC~1~`` and ``variableDeclarationIR``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+=+ expression~init~`` be ``initializerOpt``.

  ... Let ``typeIR`` and fresh type variables ``typeId^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Type_ok[typing ``type``, under context ``TC~0~`` at ``p``].
  ... Check that ``typeId^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

  ... Let ``bound'`` be xref:bound[bound type variables from the ``p`` layer of ``TC~0~``].
  ... If xref:Type_wf[``typeIR`` is a well-formed type, with bound type variables ``bound'``]:
   .... Check that xref:is_assignable_typeIR[``typeIR`` supports assignment].

   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR~init~`` be the result of xref:Expr_ok[typing ``expression~init~``, under context ``TC~0~`` at ``p``].
   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR~init_cast~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:cast_unary[``typedExpressionIR~init~`` implicitly cast to ``typeIR``].
   .... Let ``nameIR`` be xref:name[the name of ``name``].
   .... Let ``TC~1~`` be xref:add_var_t[``TC~0~`` where ``nameIR`` to ``+INOUT+ typeIR +DYN+ ·`` is added to the ``p`` layer].
   .... Let ``variableDeclarationIR`` be ``annotationList typeIR nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR~init_cast~ +;+``.
   .... Result in context ``TC~1~`` and ``variableDeclarationIR``.

