xref:Call_convention_expr_ok[Call_convention_expr_ok]:

* Checking calling convention of ``typedExpressionIR~arg~`` applied to ``++_++ direction typeIR~param~ ++_++ ++_++``, under context ``TC`` and action context ``actctxt`` at ``p``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``direction`` matches pattern ``+IN+``.

  ... Let ``typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:cast_unary[``typedExpressionIR~arg~`` implicitly cast to ``typeIR~param~``].
  ... Result in casted ``typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``direction`` is equal to ``+OUT+`` or ``direction`` is equal to ``+INOUT+``.

  ... Let ``typeIR~arg~`` be xref:type_of_typedExpressionIR[the type of ``typedExpressionIR~arg~``].
  ... If xref:Type_alpha[``typeIR~param~`` and ``typeIR~arg~`` are the same type]:
   .... Let ``typedLvalueIR~arg~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:typedExpressionIR_as_typedLvalueIR[the l-value form of ``typedExpressionIR~arg~``].
   .... Let ``lvalue~arg~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:lift_typedLvalueIR[$lift_typedLvalueIR(typedLvalueIR~arg~)]``.
   .... Let ``++_++`` be the result of xref:Lvalue_ok[typing ``lvalue~arg~``, under context ``TC`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in casted ``typedExpressionIR~arg~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``actctxt`` matches pattern ``+ACTION+``:
   .... Check that ``direction`` matches pattern ````.

   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:cast_unary[``typedExpressionIR~arg~`` implicitly cast to ``typeIR~param~``].
   .... Result in casted ``typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~``.
  ... Else:
   .... Check that ``direction`` matches pattern ````.

   .... Let ``typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:cast_unary[``typedExpressionIR~arg~`` implicitly cast to ``typeIR~param~``].
   .... Check that ``+DYN+`` is not equal to xref:ctk_of_typedExpressionIR[the compile-time known-ness of ``typedExpressionIR~arg~``].

   .... Result in casted ``typedExpressionIR~arg_cast~``.

xref:Call_convention_arg_ok[Call_convention_arg_ok]:

* Checking calling convention of ``argumentIR`` applied to parameter type ``parameterIR``, under context ``TC`` and action context ``actctxt`` at ``p``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``typedExpressionIR`` be ``argumentIR``.

  ... Let casted ``typedExpressionIR~cast~`` be the result of xref:Call_convention_expr_ok[checking calling convention of ``typedExpressionIR`` applied to ``parameterIR``, under context ``TC`` and action context ``actctxt`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in casted ``typedExpressionIR~cast~``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR`` be ``argumentIR``:
   .... Let casted ``typedExpressionIR~cast~`` be the result of xref:Call_convention_expr_ok[checking calling convention of ``typedExpressionIR`` applied to ``parameterIR``, under context ``TC`` and action context ``actctxt`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in casted ``nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR~cast~``.
  ... Else if let ``nameIR +=+ +_+`` be ``argumentIR``:
   .... Let ``++_++ direction ++_++ ++_++ ++_++`` be ``parameterIR``.
   .... Check that ``direction`` matches pattern ``+OUT+``.

   .... Result in casted ``nameIR +=+ +_+``.
  ... Else if ``argumentIR`` matches pattern ``+_+``:
   .... Let ``++_++ direction ++_++ ++_++ ++_++`` be ``parameterIR``.
   .... Check that ``direction`` matches pattern ``+OUT+``.

   .... Result in casted ``+_+``.

xref:Call_convention_ok[Call_convention_ok]:

* Checking calling convention of ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` applied on ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``TC`` and action context ``actctxt`` at ``p``.

