. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PACKAGE+``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER_STATE+``.

xref:instantiable_control[$instantiable_control(cursor, TC, instctxt)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Return ``instctxt`` is equal to ``+ANON+``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PACKAGE+``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+``.

xref:instantiable_package[$instantiable_package(cursor, TC, instctxt)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``true``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PACKAGE+``.
. Else: return ``false``.

xref:instantiable_table[$instantiable_table(cursor, TC, instctxt)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else: return ``false``.

xref:instantiable[$instantiable(p, TC, instctxt, typeIR)]

. Let ``typeIR~unroll~`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR`` with typedefs unrolled].
. If ``typeIR~unroll~`` has type ``externObjectTypeIR``:
 .. Return ``xref:instantiable_extern[$instantiable_extern(p, TC, instctxt)]``.
. Else if ``typeIR~unroll~`` has type ``parserObjectTypeIR``:
 .. Return ``xref:instantiable_parser[$instantiable_parser(p, TC, instctxt)]``.
. Else if ``typeIR~unroll~`` has type ``controlObjectTypeIR``:
 .. Return ``xref:instantiable_control[$instantiable_control(p, TC, instctxt)]``.
. Else if ``typeIR~unroll~`` has type ``packageObjectTypeIR``:
 .. Return ``xref:instantiable_package[$instantiable_package(p, TC, instctxt)]``.
. Else if ``typeIR~unroll~`` has type ``tableObjectTypeIR``:
 .. Return ``xref:instantiable_table[$instantiable_table(p, TC, instctxt)]``.

xref:callable_action[$callable_action(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+ACTION+`` or ``localKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+``.

xref:callable_definedFunction[$callable_definedFunction(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` does not have type ``externMethodLocalKind``.

xref:callable_externFunction[$callable_externFunction(cursor, TC, nameIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. If ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"verify"``: return ``false``.
 .. Else: return ``true``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. If ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"verify"``:
  ... Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
  ... Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
  ... Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else:
 .. If ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"verify"``:
  ... Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
  ... Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER_STATE+``.
 .. Else: return ``true``.

xref:callable_externMethod[$callable_externMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``blockKind`` be ``TC.+BLOCK+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER+`` or ``blockKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL+``.
. Else: return ``true``.

xref:callable_parserApplyMethod[$callable_parserApplyMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+PARSER_STATE+``.

xref:callable_controlApplyMethod[$callable_controlApplyMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+``.

xref:callable_tableApplyMethod[$callable_tableApplyMethod(cursor, TC)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``: return ``false``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``: return ``false``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``localKind`` be ``TC.+LOCAL+.+KIND+``.
 .. Return ``localKind`` is equal to ``+CONTROL_APPLY_METHOD+`` or ``localKind`` is equal to ``+TABLE_APPLY_METHOD+``.

xref:callableId_IR[The callable identifier for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``]

. Let ``++_++ ++_++ ++_++ id ++_++`` be ``parameterIR``, for all ``parameterIR`` in ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, ``++_++`` in ``++_++``, and ``id`` in ``id^{asterisk}^``.
. Return ``nameIR +(+id^{asterisk}^+)+``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_callableDef[$parameterListIR_of_callableDef(callableDef)]

. If let ``actionDef`` be ``callableDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_actionDef[$parameterListIR_of_actionDef(actionDef)]``.
. Else if let ``functionDef`` be ``callableDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_functionDef[$parameterListIR_of_functionDef(functionDef)]``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_methodDef[$parameterListIR_of_methodDef(methodDef)]``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_actionDef[$parameterListIR_of_actionDef(annotationList +ACTION+ ++_++ +(+parameterListIR+)+ ++_++)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_functionDef[$parameterListIR_of_functionDef(functionDef)]

. If let ``definedFunctionDef`` be ``functionDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef(definedFunctionDef)]``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef(externFunctionDef)]``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_definedFunctionDef(+FUNCTION+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ ++_++)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef[$parameterListIR_of_externFunctionDef(+EXTERN_FUNCTION+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_methodDef[$parameterListIR_of_methodDef(methodDef)]

. If let ``externMethodDef`` be ``methodDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef(externMethodDef)]``.
. Else if let ``parserApplyMethodDef`` be ``methodDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef(parserApplyMethodDef)]``.
. Else if let ``controlApplyMethodDef`` be ``methodDef``:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef(controlApplyMethodDef)]``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``xref:parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef(tableApplyMethodDef)]``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_externMethodDef(externMethodDef)]

. Let!~type~ ``+EXTERN_METHOD+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ ++_++^?^`` be ``externMethodDef``.

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_parserApplyMethodDef(+PARSER_APPLY+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ +;+ ++_+++}+)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_controlApplyMethodDef(+CONTROL_APPLY+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ +;+ ++_++ +;+ ++_+++}+)]

. Return ``parameterListIR``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef[$parameterListIR_of_tableApplyMethodDef(+TABLE_APPLY+ +{+++_+++}+)]

. Return ``·``.

xref:parameterListIR_of_constructorDef[$parameterListIR_of_constructorDef(constructorDef)]

. If let ``+EXTERN+ ++_++ +<+++_+++>+ +(+constructorParameterListIR+)+ +{+++_+++}+`` be ``constructorDef``:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.
. Else if let ``+PARSER+ +<+++_+++>+ +(+++_+++)+ +(+constructorParameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ ++_+++}+`` be ``constructorDef``:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.
. Else if let ``+CONTROL+ +<+++_+++>+ +(+++_+++)+ +(+constructorParameterListIR+)+ +{+++_++ +APPLY+ ++_+++}+`` be ``constructorDef``:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``constructorParameterListIR``.

xref:init_objectState[Initialization of ``nameIR````+<+`` ``typeIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+>+````+(+`` ``id^{asterisk}^`` ``+=+`` ``value^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` in the target]

xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_constructorDefEnv[$empty_constructorDefEnv]

. Return xref:empty_map[an empty map].

xref:empty_store[An empty store]

. Let ``store`` be xref:empty_map[an empty map].
. Return ``store``.

xref:add_store[``store`` where ``objectId`` to ``object`` is added]

. Let ``store'`` be xref:add_map[``store`` where ``objectId`` to ``object`` is added].
. Return ``store'``.

xref:find_store[The object ``objectId`` in ``store``]

. Let ``object`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``objectId`` in map ``store``].
. Return ``object``.

xref:empty_instContext[An empty instantiation context]

. Let ``globalInstLayer`` be +{++CONSTRUCTOR+ ``xref:empty_constructorDefEnv[$empty_constructorDefEnv]``, +TYPE+ ``xref:empty_typeDefEnv[$empty_typeDefEnv]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``blockInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +STATE+ ``xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``localInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
. Let ``IC`` be +{++PATH+ ``·``, +GLOBAL+ ``globalInstLayer``, +BLOCK+ ``blockInstLayer``, +LOCAL+ ``localInstLayer``+}+.
. Return ``IC``.

xref:enter_i[``IC`` with a new local frame]

. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame] {two-colons} IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

xref:exit_i[``IC`` with the innermost frame removed]

. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:enter_path_i[``IC`` with ``id`` added to the path]

. Return ``IC`` with ``+PATH+`` set to ``IC.+PATH+ {pp} id``.

xref:inherit_i[An instantiation context same as ``IC`` up to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``blockInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +STATE+ ``xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Let ``localInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Return ``IC[+BLOCK+ = blockInstLayer]`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``localInstLayer``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``localInstLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``localInstLayer``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``IC``.

xref:add_var_i[``IC`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, value>(IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+))]``.

 .. Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, value>(IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+))]``.

 .. Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, $dom_map<id, value>(frame~h~))]``.

 .. Let ``frame~h'~`` be xref:add_map[``frame~h~`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~h'~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:add_vars_i[``IC`` where each of ``id^{asterisk}^`` to each of ``value^{asterisk}^`` are added to the ``p`` layer]

. If ``id^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``value^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``IC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``value~h~ {two-colons} value~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``value^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``IC'`` be xref:add_var_i[``IC`` where ``id~h~`` to ``value~h~`` is added to the ``p`` layer].
 .. Let ``IC''`` be xref:add_vars_i[``IC'`` where each of ``id~t~^{asterisk}^`` to each of ``value~t~^{asterisk}^`` are added to the ``p`` layer].
 .. Return ``IC''``.

xref:add_typeDef_i[``IC`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeDefIR`` is added to the ``cursor`` layer]

. Check that ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``.

. Let ``typeDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeDefIR`` is added].
. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+`` set to ``typeDefEnv``.

xref:add_parserState_i[``IC`` where ``nameIR`` to ``parserStateIR`` is added]

. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<nameIR>(nameIR, $dom_map<nameIR, parserStateIR>(IC.+BLOCK+.+STATE+))]``.

. Let ``stateEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+STATE+`` where ``nameIR`` to ``parserStateIR`` is added].
. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+STATE+`` set to ``stateEnv``.

xref:add_type_i[$add_type_i(cursor, IC, typeId, typeIR)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``theta`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeIR`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+TYPE+`` set to ``theta``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+LOCAL+``:
 .. Let ``theta`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+LOCAL+.+TYPE+`` where ``typeId`` to ``typeIR`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+TYPE+`` set to ``theta``.

xref:add_types_i[$add_types_i(p, IC, typeId^{asterisk}^, typeIR^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``typeId^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``typeIR^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``IC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``typeIR~h~ {two-colons} typeIR~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``typeIR^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``IC'`` be ``xref:add_type_i[$add_type_i(p, IC, typeId~h~, typeIR~h~)]``.
 .. Return ``xref:add_types_i[$add_types_i(p, IC', typeId~t~^{asterisk}^, typeIR~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.

xref:add_callableDef_overload_i[``IC`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added as an overloaded callable to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<callableId>(callableId, $dom_map<callableId, callableDef>(IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+))]``.

 .. Let ``callableDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+`` set to ``callableDefEnv``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<callableId>(callableId, $dom_map<callableId, callableDef>(IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+))]``.

 .. Let ``callableDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+`` set to ``callableDefEnv``.

xref:add_callableDef_non_overload_i[``IC`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added as a non-overloaded callable to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``id +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``callableId``.
 .. Let ``+{+( id~k~ +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be xref:dom_map[the domain of the map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+``].
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, +{+id~k~^{asterisk}^+}+)]``.

 .. Let ``callableDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+`` set to ``callableDefEnv``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``id +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``callableId``.
 .. Let ``+{+( id~k~ +(+++_++^{asterisk}^+)+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be xref:dom_map[the domain of the map ``IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+``].
 .. Check that ``~xref:in_set[$in_set<id>(id, +{+id~k~^{asterisk}^+}+)]``.

 .. Let ``callableDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+`` where ``callableId`` to ``callableDef`` is added].
 .. Return ``IC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+`` set to ``callableDefEnv``.

xref:find_callableDef_non_overload_i[The non-overloaded callable definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p'`` layer of ``IC``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+.+ nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<callableDef>(IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+, nameIR)]``.

    ..... Return ``·``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let ``( callableId, callableDef )`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<callableDef>(IC.+GLOBAL+.+CALLABLE+, nameIR)]``.
    ..... Return ( ``+GLOBAL+``, ``callableId``, ``callableDef`` ).
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Return xref:find_callableDef_non_overload_i[the non-overloaded callable definition of ``+.+ nameIR`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer of ``IC``].
  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let ``( callableId, callableDef )`` be xref:option_get[*!*] ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<callableDef>(IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+, nameIR)]``.
     ...... Return ( ``+BLOCK+``, ``callableId``, ``callableDef`` ).
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``xref:find_non_overloaded[$find_non_overloaded<callableDef>(IC.+BLOCK+.+CALLABLE+, nameIR)]``.

     ...... Return xref:find_callableDef_non_overload_i[the non-overloaded callable definition of ``nameIR`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer of ``IC``].
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Return xref:find_callableDef_non_overload_i[the non-overloaded callable definition of ``nameIR`` from the ``+BLOCK+`` layer of ``IC``].

xref:add_constructorDef_i[Where ``callableId`` to ``constructorDef`` is added to ``IC``]

. Let ``constructorDefEnv`` be xref:add_map[``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CONSTRUCTOR+`` where ``callableId`` to ``constructorDef`` is added].
. Return ``IC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+CONSTRUCTOR+`` set to ``constructorDefEnv``.

xref:add_constructorDefs_i[Where each of ``callableId^{asterisk}^`` to each of ``constructorDef^{asterisk}^`` are added to ``IC``]

. If ``callableId^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``constructorDef^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``IC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``constructorDef~h~ {two-colons} constructorDef~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``constructorDef^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``IC'`` be xref:add_constructorDef_i[where ``callableId~h~`` to ``constructorDef~h~`` is added to ``IC``].
 .. Let ``IC''`` be xref:add_constructorDefs_i[where each of ``callableId~t~^{asterisk}^`` to each of ``constructorDef~t~^{asterisk}^`` are added to ``IC'``].
 .. Return ``IC''``.

xref:find_var_i[The value of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p'`` layer of ``IC``]

. If let ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``].
 .. Return ``value``.
. Else:
 .. If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
  ... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``].
  ... Return ``value``.
 .. Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``].
    ..... Return ``value``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``IC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``].

    ..... Return xref:find_var_i[the value of ``id`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer of ``IC``].
 .. Else:
  ... Try:
   .... {empty}
    ..... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_maps[the value of ``id`` in maps ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``].
    ..... Return ``value``.
   .... {empty}
    ..... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:find_maps[the value of ``id`` in maps ``IC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``].

    ..... Return xref:find_var_i[the value of ``id`` from the ``+BLOCK+`` layer of ``IC``].

xref:find_typeDef_i[The type definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``++_++`` layer of ``IC``]

. If let ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Return xref:find_map[the value of ``nameIR`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+``].
. Else:
 .. Return xref:find_map[the value of ``nameIR`` in map ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+TYPE+``].

xref:find_constructorDef_i[The overloaded constructor definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+`` in ``IC``]

. If let ``nameIR`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
 .. Return xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CONSTRUCTOR+`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_constructorDef``].
. Else:
 .. Let ``callTargetKey`` be xref:callTargetKey[the call target key for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``argumentIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].
 .. Return xref:find_overloaded[finding the item in ``IC.+GLOBAL+.+CONSTRUCTOR+`` matching ``callTargetKey`` using parameter getter ``$parameterListIR_of_constructorDef``].

xref:subst_type_i[``typeIR`` substituted by bound type variables in ``IC`` from the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Return ``typeIR``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``theta`` be ``IC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``typeIR~subst~`` be xref:subst_typeIR[``typeIR`` substituted by ``theta``].
 .. Return ``typeIR~subst~``.
. Else:
 .. Let ``theta~block~`` be ``IC.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``theta~local~`` be ``IC.+LOCAL+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``theta`` be ``xref:extend_map[$extend_map<typeId, typeIR>(theta~block~, theta~local~)]``.
 .. Let ``typeIR~subst~`` be xref:subst_typeIR[``typeIR`` substituted by ``theta``].
 .. Return ``typeIR~subst~``.

xref:Expr_inst[Expr_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of xref:typedExpressionIR[``expressionIR`` annotated with ``++_++``], under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``.

. If let ``booleanLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let ``boolValue`` be xref:ite[``true`` if ``booleanLiteral`` is equal to ``+TRUE+`` otherwise ``false``].
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``boolValue``.
. Else if let ``integerLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``integerLiteral``.
. Else if let ``stringLiteral`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``stringLiteral``.
. Else if let ``prefixedNameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let ``value`` be xref:find_var_i[the value of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p`` layer of ``IC``].
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``value``.
. Else if let ``defaultExpression`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Check that ``defaultExpression`` matches pattern ``+...+``.

 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``+DEFAULT+``.
. Else if let ``unop typedExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~1~`` and xref:un_op[``unop`` ``value``].
. Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~l~ binop typedExpressionIR~r~`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``binop`` is not in ``+[+ +&&+, +||+ +]+``.

   .... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~l~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
   .... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and xref:bin_op[``value~l~`` ``binop`` ``value~r~``].
  ... {empty}
   .... If ``binop`` matches pattern ``+&&+``:
    ..... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
    ..... Try:
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``false``.
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

      ....... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~``.
   .... Else if ``binop`` matches pattern ``+||+``:
    ..... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~l~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
    ..... Try:
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``true``.
     ...... {empty}
      ....... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

      ....... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~r~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~r~``.
. Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~cond~ +?+ typedExpressionIR~true~ +:+ typedExpressionIR~false~`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~cond~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``true``.

   .... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~true~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~true~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~true~``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Check that ``value`` is equal to ``false``.

   .... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~false~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~false~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~false~``.
. Else if let ``+(+typeIR+)+ typedExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Let ``value~cast~`` be xref:cast_op[``value`` casted to type ``typeIR``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~cast~``.
. Else if let ``invalidHeaderExpression`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Check that ``invalidHeaderExpression`` matches pattern ``+{#}+``.

 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``+{#}+``.
. Else if let ``sequenceExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. If let ``+SEQ+ +{+typedExpressionListIR+}+`` be ``sequenceExpressionIR``:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionListIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^+)+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionListIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+SEQ+ +(+value^{asterisk}^ +,+ +...++)+``.
. Else if let ``recordExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. If let ``+RECORD+ +{+( nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``recordExpressionIR``:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+RECORD+ +{+( value nameIR +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``+RECORD+ +{+( value nameIR +;+ )^{asterisk}^ +,+ +...++}+``.
. Else if let ``+ERROR+ +.+ nameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let ``nameIR~error~`` be ``"error."`` concatenated with ``nameIR``.
 .. Let ``value~error~`` be xref:find_var_i[the value of ``nameIR~error~`` from the ``p`` layer of ``IC``].
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``value~error~``.
. Else if let ``memberAccessBaseIR +.+ nameIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Try:
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``+TYPE+ prefixedNameIR`` be ``memberAccessBaseIR``.

   .... Let ``typeDefIR~base~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_typeDef_i[the type definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p`` layer of ``IC``].
   .... Let ``typeIR~base~`` be xref:typeIR_of_typeDefIR[the underlying type of ``typeDefIR~base~``].
   .... Let ``typeIR`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR~base~`` with typedefs unrolled].
   .... If let ``+ENUM+ typeId +{+++_++^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR``:
    ..... Result in store ``STO'`` and ``typeId +.+ nameIR``.
   .... Else if let ``+ENUM+ typeId +<+++_+++>+ +{+( id~member~ +=+ value~member~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``typeIR``:
    ..... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``( id~member~, value~member~ )^{asterisk}^``].
    ..... Result in store ``STO'`` and ``typeId +.+ nameIR +.+ value``.
  ... {empty}
   .... Let!~type~ ``typedExpressionIR~base~`` be ``memberAccessBaseIR``.

   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let ``typeIR~base~`` be xref:type_of_typedExpressionIR[the type of ``typedExpressionIR~base~``].
     ...... Let ``typeIR`` be xref:unroll_typeIR[``typeIR~base~`` with typedefs unrolled].
     ...... Let!~type~ ``+HEADER_STACK+ ++_++ +[+n~size~+]+`` be ``typeIR``.

     ...... Check that ``nameIR`` is equal to ``"size"``.

     ...... Result in store ``STO'`` and ``32 +W+ n~size~``.
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value'`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~base~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
     ...... If let ``structValue`` be ``value'``:
      ....... Let ``+STRUCT+ ++_++ +{+( value~field~ id~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``structValue``.
      ....... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``( id~field~, value~field~ )^{asterisk}^``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.
     ...... Else if let ``headerValue`` be ``value'``:
      ....... Let ``+HEADER+ ++_++ +{+++_++ +;+ ( value~field~ id~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``headerValue``.
      ....... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``( id~field~, value~field~ )^{asterisk}^``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.
     ...... Else if let ``headerUnionValue`` be ``value'``:
      ....... Let ``+HEADER_UNION+ ++_++ +{+( value~field~ id~field~ +;+ )^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``headerUnionValue``.
      ....... Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:assoc_[the value associated to ``nameIR`` in ``( id~field~, value~field~ )^{asterisk}^``].
      ....... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.
. Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~base~ +[+typedExpressionIR~index~+]+`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~base~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~base~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value'`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~index~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``integerValue~index~`` be ``value'``.

 .. If let ``+TUPLE+ +(+value~e~^{asterisk}^+)+`` be ``value~base~``:
  ... Let ``n~index~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~index~``].
  ... Check that ``n~index~`` is less than the length of ``value~e~^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``value`` be ``value~e~^{asterisk}^[n~index~]``.
  ... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value``.
 .. Else if let ``+ARRAY+ +[+value~e~^{asterisk}^+]+`` be ``value~base~``:
  ... Let ``n~index~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~index~``].
  ... Check that ``n~index~`` is less than the length of ``value~e~^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``value`` be ``value~e~^{asterisk}^[n~index~]``.
  ... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value``.
 .. Else if let ``+HEADER_STACK+ +[+value~e~^{asterisk}^ +(+++_+++)++]+`` be ``value~base~``:
  ... Let ``n~index~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:nat_of_integerValue[the natural number representation of  ``integerValue~index~``].
  ... Check that ``n~index~`` is less than the length of ``value~e~^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let ``value`` be ``value~e~^{asterisk}^[n~index~]``.
  ... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value``.
. Else if let ``typedExpressionIR~base~ +[+typedExpressionIR~hi~ sliceop typedExpressionIR~lo~+]+`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. If ``sliceop`` matches pattern ``+:+``:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~base~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~base~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~hi~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~hi~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
  ... Let store ``STO~3~`` and ``value~lo~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~lo~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~2~`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~3~`` and <<bitacc_range_op,``value~base~`` ``+[+`` ``value~hi~`` ``+:+`` ``value~lo~`` ``+]+``>>.
 .. Else:
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~base~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~base~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~l~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~hi~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
  ... Let store ``STO~3~`` and ``value~w~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~lo~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~2~`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~3~`` and <<bitacc_offset_op,``value~base~`` ``+[+`` ``value~l~`` ``++:+`` ``value~w~`` ``+]+``>>.
. Else if let ``callExpressionIR`` be ``expressionIR``:
 .. If let ``prefixedNameIR +<+typeArgumentListIR+>+ +(+argumentListIR+)+`` be ``callExpressionIR``:
  ... Let constructor ``constructorDef`` ``+<+`` ``typeArgumentListIR~inst~`` ``+>+`` with defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Constructor_inst[finding constructor for ``prefixedNameIR`` ``+<+`` ``typeArgumentListIR`` ``+>+`` ``+(+`` ``argumentListIR`` ``+)+`` under context ``IC`` at ``p``].
  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and instantiated ``object`` be the result of xref:Constructor_call[instantiating ``constructorDef`` ``+<+`` ``typeArgumentListIR~inst~`` ``+>+`` ``+(+`` ``argumentListIR`` ``+)+`` with defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
  ... Let ``STO~2~`` be xref:add_store[``STO~1~`` where ``IC.+PATH+`` to ``object`` is added].
  ... Let ``value~ref~`` be ``+REF+ IC.+PATH+``.
  ... Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~ref~``.
 .. Else:
  ... If let ``typedExpressionIR~base~ +.+ nameIR`` be ``callableTargetIR``:
   .... Let ``++_++ +#+ +(+typeIR~base~ ++_+++)+`` be ``typedExpressionIR~base~``.
   .... Check that ``nameIR`` is in ``+[+ "minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes" +]+``.

   .... Result in store ``STO'`` and ``xref:sizeof[$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)]``.
  ... Else if let ``+TYPE+ prefixedNameIR +.+ nameIR`` be ``callableTargetIR``:
   .... Let ``typeDefIR~base~`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_typeDef_i[the type definition of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p`` layer of ``IC``].
   .... If xref:is_monomorphic_typeDefIR[``typeDefIR~base~`` is monomorphic]:
    ..... Let ``typeIR~base~`` be xref:typeIR_of_typeDefIR[the underlying type of ``typeDefIR~base~``].
    ..... Check that ``nameIR`` is in ``+[+ "minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes" +]+``.

    ..... Result in store ``STO'`` and ``xref:sizeof[$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)]``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Check that ( ``·``, ``·`` ) is equal to xref:typeParameterListIR_of_typeDefIR[the type parameters of ``typeDefIR~base~``].

    ..... Let ``typeIR~base~`` be xref:typeIR_of_typeDefIR[the underlying type of ``typeDefIR~base~``].
    ..... Check that ``nameIR`` is in ``+[+ "minSizeInBits", "minSizeInBytes", "maxSizeInBits", "maxSizeInBytes" +]+``.

    ..... Result in store ``STO'`` and ``xref:sizeof[$sizeof(typeIR~base~, nameIR)]``.
  ... Else if let ``+(+callableTargetIR+)+`` be ``callableTargetIR``:
   .... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``callableTargetIR +<+++_+++>+ +(+++_+++)+`` annotated with ``++_++``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
   .... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.
. Else:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.

xref:Exprs_inst[Exprs_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``.

. If ``typedExpressionIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``·``.
. Else:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value~h~`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~h~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~t~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Exprs_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR~t~^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``value~h~ {two-colons} value~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:Argument_inst[Argument_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of ``argumentIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~0~`` at ``p``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``typedExpressionIR`` be ``argumentIR``.

  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~0~`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``nameIR +=+ typedExpressionIR`` be ``argumentIR``.

  ... Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``value`` be the result of xref:Expr_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``typedExpressionIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~0~`` at ``p``].
  ... Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``value``.

xref:DirectApplicationStmt_inst[DirectApplicationStmt_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of ``constructorTargetIR +.+ +APPLY+ +(+argumentListIR+)+ +;+``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~0~`` at ``p``.

. Let ``prefixedNameIR +<+typeArgumentListIR+>+`` be ``constructorTargetIR``.
. Let constructor ``constructorDef`` ``+<+`` ``typeArgumentListIR~inst~`` ``+>+`` with defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:Constructor_inst[finding constructor for ``prefixedNameIR`` ``+<+`` ``typeArgumentListIR`` ``+>+`` ``+(+`` ``·`` ``+)+`` under context ``IC`` at ``p``].
. Let ``typeId`` be xref:flatten_prefixedNameIR[the string form of  ``prefixedNameIR``].
. Let ``IC~callee~`` be xref:enter_path_i[``IC`` with ``typeId`` added to the path].
. Let store ``STO~1~`` and instantiated ``object`` be the result of xref:Constructor_call[instantiating ``constructorDef`` ``+<+`` ``typeArgumentListIR~inst~`` ``+>+`` ``+(+`` ``·`` ``+)+`` with defaults ``id~default~^{asterisk}^`` and optionals ``id~optional~^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC~callee~`` and store ``STO~0~`` at ``p``].
. Let ``typeId~fresh~`` be xref:fresh_typeId[a fresh type variable].
. Let ``typeIR`` be ``typeId``.
. Let ``nameIR`` be <<concat_text,the concatenation of ``+[+ typeId, "_", typeId~fresh~ +]+``>>.
. Let ``objectId`` be ``IC.+PATH+`` concatenated with ``typeId``.
. Let ``STO~2~`` be xref:add_store[``STO~1~`` where ``objectId`` to ``object`` is added].
. Let ``constantDeclarationIR`` be ``+CONST+ typeIR nameIR +=+ +REF+ objectId +;+``.
. Let ``typedExpressionIR~base~`` be xref:typedExpressionIR[``nameIR`` annotated with a pair of type ``typeIR`` and compile-time known-ness ``+CTK+``].
. Let ``callableTargetIR`` be ``typedExpressionIR~base~ +.+ "apply"``.
. Let ``callStatementIR`` be ``callableTargetIR +<+typeArgumentListIR~inst~+>+ +(+argumentListIR+)+ +;+``.
. Result in store ``STO~2~`` and desugared ``constantDeclarationIR``, ``callStatementIR``.

xref:Stmt_inst[Stmt_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of ``statementIR''``, under context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p'``.

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... If let ``emptyStatementIR`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO'``, and ``emptyStatementIR``.
  ... Else if let ``assignmentStatementIR`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO'``, and ``assignmentStatementIR``.
  ... Else if let ``callStatementIR`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO'``, and ``callStatementIR``.
  ... Else if let ``directApplicationStatementIR`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... Let store ``STO~1~`` and desugared ``constantDeclarationIR``, ``callStatementIR`` be the result of xref:DirectApplicationStmt_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``directApplicationStatementIR``, under context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p'``].
   .... Let ``blockStatementIR`` be ``+{++[+ constantDeclarationIR, callStatementIR +]++}+``.
   .... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO~1~``, and ``blockStatementIR``.
  ... Else if let ``exitStatementIR`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO'``, and ``exitStatementIR``.
  ... Else if let ``conditionalStatementIR`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... If let ``+IF+ +(+typedExpressionIR~cond~+)+ statementIR~then~`` be ``conditionalStatementIR``:
    ..... Let context ``IC~then~``, store ``STO~1~``, and ``statementIR~then_inst~`` be the result of xref:Stmt_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``statementIR~then~``, under context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p'``].
    ..... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO~1~``, and ``+IF+ +(+typedExpressionIR~cond~+)+ statementIR~then_inst~``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Let context ``IC~then~``, store ``STO~1~``, and ``statementIR~then_inst~`` be the result of xref:Stmt_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``statementIR~then~``, under context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p'``].
    ..... Let context ``IC~else~``, store ``STO~2~``, and ``statementIR~else_inst~`` be the result of xref:Stmt_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``statementIR~else~``, under context ``IC'`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p'``].
    ..... Result in context ``IC'``, store ``STO~2~``, and ``+IF+ +(+typedExpressionIR~cond~+)+ statementIR~then_inst~ +ELSE+ statementIR~else_inst~``.
  ... Else if let ``forStatementIR'`` be ``statementIR''``:
   .... If let ``annotationList +FOR+ +(+forInitStatementListIR +;+ typedExpressionIR +;+ forUpdateStatementListIR+)+ statementIR`` be ``forStatementIR'``:
