 .. Let store ``STO~2~`` and context ``IC~callee_3~`` be the result of xref:Copy_in_inst_default[copying defaults ``constructorParameterIR~default~^{asterisk}^`` from ``p`` at ``IC`` to ``IC~callee_2~`` at ``p~callee~``, under store ``STO~1~``].
 .. Let ``theta~package~`` be ``IC~callee_3~.+BLOCK+.+TYPE+``.
 .. Let ``frame~package~`` be ``IC~callee_3~.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``.
 .. Let ``object~package~`` be ``+PACKAGE+ +<+theta~package~+>+ +{+frame~package~+}+``.
 .. Result in store ``STO~2~`` and instantiated ``object~package~``.

xref:SwitchCase_inst[SwitchCase_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of ``switchCaseIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~0'~`` at ``p``.

. If let ``switchLabelIR +:+ blockStatementIR`` be ``switchCaseIR``:
 .. Let context ``IC~switch~``, store ``STO~1~``, and ``statementIR`` be the result of xref:Stmt_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``blockStatementIR``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~0'~`` at ``p``].
 .. Let!~type~ ``blockStatementIR~inst~`` be ``statementIR``.

 .. Result in store ``STO~1~`` and ``switchLabelIR +:+ blockStatementIR~inst~``.
. Else:
 .. Result in store ``STO~0'~`` and ``switchLabelIR +:+``.

xref:SwitchCases_inst[SwitchCases_inst]:

* Compile-time evaluation of ``switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``.

. If ``switchCaseIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Result in store ``STO'`` and ``·``.
. Else:
 .. Let store ``STO~1~`` and ``switchCaseIR~h'~`` be the result of xref:SwitchCase_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``switchCaseIR~h~``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO'`` at ``p``].
 .. Let store ``STO~2~`` and ``switchCaseIR~t'~^{asterisk}^`` be the result of xref:SwitchCases_inst[compile-time evaluation of ``switchCaseIR~t~^{asterisk}^``, under context ``IC`` and store ``STO~1~`` at ``p``].
 .. Result in store ``STO~2~`` and ``switchCaseIR~h'~ {two-colons} switchCaseIR~t'~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:merge_frames[The merged frame of ``frame`` and ``+{+( id +:+ value )^{asterisk}^+}+``]

. Return xref:adds_map[``frame`` where each of ``id^{asterisk}^`` to ``value^{asterisk}^`` are added].

xref:merge_externMethodDefEnvs[The merged extern method definition environment of ``externMethodDefEnv`` and ``set<pair<callableId, callableDef>>'``]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``set<pair<callableId, callableDef>>'`` is equal to ``+{+·+}+``.

  ... Return ``externMethodDefEnv``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``+{+pair<callableId, callableDef>^{asterisk}^+}+`` be ``set<pair<callableId, callableDef>>'``.
  ... Let!~type~ ``callableId~h~ +:+ callableDef~h~ {two-colons} ( callableId~t~ +:+ callableDef~t~ )^{asterisk}^`` be ``pair<callableId, callableDef>^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``+FUNCTION+ nameIR +<+typeParameterListIR+>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ blockStatementIR`` be ``callableDef~h~``.

  ... Let ``externMethodDef~h~`` be ``+EXTERN_METHOD+ nameIR +<+typeParameterListIR+>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ blockStatementIR``.
  ... Let ``externMethodDefEnv~post~`` be xref:update_map[the map ``externMethodDefEnv`` with the value for ``callableId~h~`` is updated to ``externMethodDef~h~``].
  ... Return xref:merge_externMethodDefEnvs[the merged extern method definition environment of ``externMethodDefEnv~post~`` and ``+{+( callableId~t~ +:+ callableDef~t~ )^{asterisk}^+}+``].

xref:ObjectDecl_inst[ObjectDecl_inst]:

* Loading ``objectDeclarationIR`` under instantiation context ``IC~0~`` and store ``STO'``.

. If let ``functionDeclarationIR`` be ``objectDeclarationIR``:
 .. Let context ``IC~1~`` be the result of xref:FuncDecl_inst[loading ``functionDeclarationIR``, under context ``IC~0~`` at ``+BLOCK+``].
 .. Result in the updated instantiation context ``IC~1~`` and store ``STO'``.
. Else:
 .. Let context ``IC~1~``, store ``STO~1~``, and reference to object ``++_++`` be the result of xref:InstDecl_inst[loading ``instantiationIR``, under context ``IC~0~`` and store ``STO'`` at ``+BLOCK+``].
 .. Result in the updated instantiation context ``IC~1~`` and store ``STO~1~``.

xref:ObjectDecls_inst[ObjectDecls_inst]:

* Loading ``objectDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`` under instantiation context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'``.

. If ``objectDeclarationIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Result in the updated instantiation context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'``.
. Else:
 .. Let the updated instantiation context ``IC~1~`` and store ``STO~1~`` be the result of xref:ObjectDecl_inst[loading ``objectDeclarationIR~h~`` under instantiation context ``IC'`` and store ``STO'``].
 .. Let the updated instantiation context ``IC~2~`` and store ``STO~2~`` be the result of xref:ObjectDecls_inst[loading ``objectDeclarationIR~t~^{asterisk}^`` under instantiation context ``IC~1~`` and store ``STO~1~``].
 .. Result in the updated instantiation context ``IC~2~`` and store ``STO~2~``.

xref:callableId_of_externMethodPrototypeIR[The callable id of  ``externMethodPrototypeIR``]

. If let ``++_++ ++_++ nameIR +<+++_++ +,+ ++_+++>+ +(+parameterListIR+)+ +;+`` be ``externMethodPrototypeIR``:
 .. Return xref:callableId_IR[the callable identifier for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``parameterListIR`` ``+)+``].
. Else:
 .. Return xref:callableId_IR[the callable identifier for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``parameterListIR`` ``+)+``].

xref:callableId_of_externConstructorPrototypeIR[The constructor id of  ``++_++ nameIR +<++,+ ++_+++>+ +(+parameterIR^{asterisk}^+)+ +;+``]

. Return xref:callableId_IR[the callable identifier for ``nameIR`` ``+(+`` ``parameterIR^{asterisk}^`` ``+)+``].

xref:constructor_of_externConstructorPrototypeIR[The constructor definition of  ``++_++ nameIR +<++,+ typeParameterListIR~impl~+>+ +(+parameterIR^{asterisk}^+)+ +;+`` with type parameters  ``typeParameterListIR~expl~``  and methods  ``externMethodPrototypeListIR``]

. Let ``typeParameterListIR`` be ``typeParameterListIR~expl~`` concatenated with ``typeParameterListIR~impl~``.
. Let ``constructorDef`` be ``+EXTERN+ nameIR +<+typeParameterListIR+>+ +(+parameterIR^{asterisk}^+)+ +{+externMethodPrototypeListIR+}+``.
. Return ``constructorDef``.

xref:init_table[$init_table(tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^)]

. Let ``tableKeysPropertyIR`` be ``xref:init_tableKeys[$init_tableKeys(tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Let ``tablePropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableActionsPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].
. Let!~type~ ``tableActionsPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be ``tablePropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

. Let!~type~ ``tableActionsPropertyIR`` be ``tableActionsPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

. Let ``tablePropertyIR''^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableDefaultActionPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].
. Let!~type~ ``tableDefaultActionPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be ``tablePropertyIR''^{asterisk}^``.

. Let!~type~ ``tableDefaultActionPropertyIR`` be ``tableDefaultActionPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

. Let ``tableEntriesPropertyIR`` be ``xref:init_tableEntries[$init_tableEntries(tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^)]``.
. Let ``tablePropertyIR'''^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableCustomPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].
. Let!~type~ ``tableCustomPropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` be ``tablePropertyIR'''^{asterisk}^``.

. Let ``TBL`` be +{++KEYS+ ``tableKeysPropertyIR``, +ACTIONS+ ``tableActionsPropertyIR``, +DEFAULT_ACTION+ ``tableDefaultActionPropertyIR``, +ENTRIES+ ``tableEntriesPropertyIR``, +CUSTOMS+ ``tableCustomPropertyIR^{asterisk}^``+}+.
. Return ``TBL``.

xref:init_tableKeys[$init_tableKeys(tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``tablePropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableKeysPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].
  ... Let!~type~ ``tableKeysPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be ``tablePropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``tableKeysPropertyIR`` be ``tableKeysPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Return ``tableKeysPropertyIR``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableKeysPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].

  ... Return ``+KEY+ +=+ +{+·+}+``.

xref:init_tableEntries[$init_tableEntries(tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^)]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let ``tablePropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableEntriesPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].
  ... Let!~type~ ``tableEntriesPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^`` be ``tablePropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Let!~type~ ``tableEntriesPropertyIR`` be ``tableEntriesPropertyIR'^{asterisk}^``.

  ... Return ``tableEntriesPropertyIR``.
 .. {empty}
  ... Check that ``·`` is equal to xref:filter_[``tablePropertyIR^{asterisk}^`` filtered by ``( tablePropertyIR has type tableEntriesPropertyIR )^{asterisk}^``].

  ... Return ``· +ENTRIES+ +=+ +{+·+}+``.

xref:enter_e[``EC`` with a new local frame]

. Return ``EC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame] {two-colons} EC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

xref:exit_e[``EC`` with the innermost frame removed]

. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``EC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

. Return ``EC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:inherit_e[Copy of ``EC`` from the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Let ``blockEvalLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +CALLABLE+ ``xref:empty_callableDefEnv[$empty_callableDefEnv]``, +STATE+ ``xref:empty_stateEnv[$empty_stateEnv]``, +FRAME+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Let ``localEvalLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Return ``EC[+BLOCK+ = blockEvalLayer]`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``localEvalLayer``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let ``localEvalLayer`` be +{++TYPE+ ``xref:empty_theta[$empty_theta]``, +FRAMES+ ``xref:empty_frame[$empty_frame]``+}+.
 .. Return ``EC`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``localEvalLayer``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``EC``.

xref:copy_e[$copy_e(cursor, EC~from~, EC~to~)]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. Return ``EC~to~`` with ``+GLOBAL+`` set to ``EC~from~.+GLOBAL+``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Return ``EC~to~[+GLOBAL+ = EC~from~.+GLOBAL+]`` with ``+BLOCK+`` set to ``EC~from~.+BLOCK+``.
. Else:
 .. Return ``EC~to~[+GLOBAL+ = EC~from~.+GLOBAL+][+BLOCK+ = EC~from~.+BLOCK+]`` with ``+LOCAL+`` set to ``EC~from~.+LOCAL+``.

xref:add_var_e[``EC`` where ``prefixedNameIR`` to ``value`` is added to the ``cursor`` layer]

. If ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
 .. If let ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
  ... Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``EC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
  ... Return ``EC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
 .. Else:
  ... Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``EC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
  ... Return ``EC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
. Else if ``cursor`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
 .. Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

 .. Let ``frame`` be xref:add_map[``EC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``EC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

 .. Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``EC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
 .. Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``frame~h'~`` be xref:add_map[``frame~h~`` where ``id`` to ``value`` is added].
 .. Return ``EC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~h'~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.

xref:add_vars_e[$add_vars_e(p, EC, prefixedNameIR^{asterisk}^, value^{asterisk}^)]

. If ``prefixedNameIR^{asterisk}^`` matches pattern ``[]``:
 .. Check that ``value^{asterisk}^`` is an empty list.

 .. Return ``EC``.
. Else:
 .. Let!~type~ ``value~h~ {two-colons} value~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``value^{asterisk}^``.

 .. Let ``EC'`` be xref:add_var_e[``EC`` where ``prefixedNameIR~h~`` to ``value~h~`` is added to the ``p`` layer].
 .. Let ``EC''`` be ``xref:add_vars_e[$add_vars_e(p, EC', prefixedNameIR~t~^{asterisk}^, value~t~^{asterisk}^)]``.
 .. Return ``EC''``.

xref:update_var_e[``EC`` where ``prefixedNameIR`` is updated to ``value`` from the ``p'`` layer]

. Try:
 .. {empty}
  ... Let!~type~ ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

  ... Let ``frame`` be xref:update_map[the map ``EC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` with the value for ``id`` is updated to ``value``].
  ... Return ``EC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame``.
 .. {empty}
  ... If ``p'`` matches pattern ``+GLOBAL+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame`` be ``EC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``.
   .... Check that xref:in_set[``id`` is an element of the set the domain of the map ``frame``].

   .... Let ``frame'`` be xref:update_map[the map ``frame`` with the value for ``id`` is updated to ``value``].
   .... Return ``EC`` with ``+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame'``.
  ... Else if ``p'`` matches pattern ``+BLOCK+``:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Let ``frame`` be ``EC.+BLOCK+.+FRAME+``.
   .... If xref:in_set[``id`` is an element of the set the domain of the map ``frame``]:
    ..... Let ``frame'`` be xref:update_map[the map ``frame`` with the value for ``id`` is updated to ``value``].
    ..... Return ``EC`` with ``+BLOCK+.+FRAME+`` set to ``frame'``.
   .... Else:
    ..... Return xref:update_var_e[``EC`` where ``id`` is updated to ``value`` from the ``+GLOBAL+`` layer].
  ... Else:
   .... Let!~type~ ``id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``.

   .... Try:
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Check that ``·`` is equal to ``EC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

     ...... Return xref:update_var_e[``EC`` where ``id`` is updated to ``value`` from the ``+BLOCK+`` layer].
    ..... {empty}
     ...... Let ``frame^{asterisk}^`` be ``EC.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.
     ...... Let!~type~ ``frame~h~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^`` be ``frame^{asterisk}^``.

     ...... If xref:in_set[``id`` is an element of the set the domain of the map ``frame~h~``]:
      ....... Let ``frame~h'~`` be xref:update_map[the map ``frame~h~`` with the value for ``id`` is updated to ``value``].
      ....... Return ``EC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~h'~ {two-colons} frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.
     ...... Else:
      ....... Let ``EC~pop~`` be ``EC`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~t~^{asterisk}^``.
      ....... Let ``EC~pop'~`` be xref:update_var_e[``EC~pop~`` where ``id`` is updated to ``value`` from the ``+LOCAL+`` layer].
      ....... Return ``EC~pop'~`` with ``+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+`` set to ``frame~h~ {two-colons} EC~pop'~.+LOCAL+.+FRAMES+``.

xref:find_var_e[The value of ``prefixedNameIR`` from the ``p'`` layer of ``EC``]

. If let ``+.+ id`` be ``prefixedNameIR``:
 .. Let ``value`` be xref:option_get[*!*] xref:find_map[the value of ``id`` in map ``EC.+GLOBAL+.+FRAME+``].
